{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_ef33a2981a9b4133bc896ec929d9d310","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_aaeb50c938b30d1eb43a048573f133afc3ef11d77e5125f031c6535936f6de5e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"jcz2020/par@4b593db4465d snapshot 8335b6fb3b4903ae","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1c34dac756d5c7f2868a0ce74265efe6c74916f14694564cce808d2ed6928b9c","slc_d99d34d1210b61dc53f162ee08ffc713b347de9e0c1933f7f8c1f233dc060b0b","slc_fa693a7a37e202334ddadff0a04a74f9a66a62e66292f776bb25c131e2dde2b0"],"source_ids":["src_e71291c5e30b5f149db5da9d32b19cb8"],"text":"When memory is configured, three builtin tools (recall_memory, remember_memory, search_history) are auto-registered and scoped per session via invoke_context.session_id.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ef33a2981a9b4133bc896ec929d9d310"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_ef33a2981a9b4133bc896ec929d9d310","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c8099bb7d88629e43b01524e418d0c8503408ca30ffca88a56a4aa6ea049e035","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"jcz2020/par@4b593db4465d snapshot 8335b6fb3b4903ae","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_bbcfd503430d522a84cba55af58957d0f5e09022b6b8c04931cea6032e21a450"],"source_ids":["src_e71291c5e30b5f149db5da9d32b19cb8"],"text":"Each Runtime has its own memory service; cross-agent knowledge sharing requires a shared SQLite file or a future remote backend, per the memory docs.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ef33a2981a9b4133bc896ec929d9d310"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_ef33a2981a9b4133bc896ec929d9d310","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_fc38c0b95d1f3b738f6983995e6d5826619227dd4b46394b29a6442b274dc80b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"jcz2020/par@4b593db4465d snapshot 8335b6fb3b4903ae","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_70b8d02ffa6e14521d1e1cea10d4ba3a3f7f65cc9ea0ad4dbe871abdf0f3f502","slc_e65200987ad26416de58476685e1746790d6d53a21fc83af112366e8fb8dbcef"],"source_ids":["src_abf0d85fbb36593aa2b315e287eb9f3e"],"text":"PAR runs its stack on Eio structured concurrency: each Runtime has an Eio switch as cancellation root, and Runtime.close cancels all fibers including tool handlers and LLM streams.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ef33a2981a9b4133bc896ec929d9d310"}
